 "parsed": {
  "count": 2,
  "rationale": "Deploying mfa:admin and mfa:dbadmin together blocks exfiltration, and no single control does. Phishing is always available, so the attacker always gets foothold_workstation and stolen_user. Without segmentation, pivot_internal then gives reach_internal. From there, auth_appserver/apiserver/ciserver work even with mfa:user, because a workstation foothold bypasses it. Kerberoasting gives stolen_admin, escalate_ciserver gives admin_ciserver, and leak_secrets_ciserver gives stolen_dbadmin. None of these steps can be blocked by any control. With both MFA controls deployed, auth_dc and auth_adfs fail, so admin_dc and admin_adfs are unreachable. auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup then fail too, leaving no exfiltration path. Each single control fails: mfa:admin alone still allows auth_db using the stolen dbadmin credential from ciserver. mfa:dbadmin alone still allows auth_dc and escalate_dc, and admin_dc bypasses mfa:dbadmin. segmented alone is bypassed by escalate_workstation. Every other control blocks only optional steps. So the minimum is 2."
 },
